; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; seiyaku.source.vla - Seiyaku (制約, "constraints"), a number-placement puzzle at rate zero
; (CART.14): eighty-one variables, twenty-seven constraints, one solution. The pass expands
; this file into seiyaku.vla beside it, the rows the engine loads (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8):
; edit this one, then expand it again with
;   cargo run --release --example expand
; Its book, the block near its end, is written by
;   cargo run --release --example seiyaku
; and never by hand.
;
; How to play. The Board is nine rows of nine variables, in nine boxes of three by three.
; Each row, each column and each box is a constraint: it holds each value from 1 to 9 once.
; The instance fixes some values, its givens, drawn in bold. Move with the arrows, Page Up
; and Page Down, Home and End, and the mouse; then, as the keys beside the Board say too:
;   1 to 9, on the row of digits or the keypad: assign the value to the variable the
;     selection stands on.
;   Backspace: retract the assignment; on an unassigned variable, strike every mark.
;   Q W E, A S D, Z X C: mark a value in the variable's domain, or strike it, each key where
;     its mark stands in the cell: Q the 1 at the top left, S the 5 in the middle, C the 9.
;   F: fill every unassigned variable's domain with the values its constraints still allow.
;   R: retract every assignment and strike every mark.
;   N: a new instance. G: the next instance's grade, 1 to 4 and round.
; A variable whose value repeats in one of its constraints is violated, and drawn red. When
; every variable is assigned and no constraint is violated, the instance is satisfied, and
; the Board turns Lovelace Lavender. The Constraints sheet keeps the counts and each
; constraint's state. Clock!B3 is the seed: everyone who types the same seed is dealt the
; same instances.
;
; The words are constraint programming's: a cell is a variable, a digit a value, an entry an
; assignment, an erasure a retraction, the pencil marks the variable's domain, a conflict a
; violated constraint, solved satisfied, and a puzzle an instance.
;
; Where the instances come from (CART.14, decisions 7 to 9). The book holds 128 puzzles, 32 a
; grade, each with one solution, written by the generator of engine/src/seiyaku.rs, which
; cargo test holds by two solvers. A grade is the hardest technique a puzzle needs: 1 naked
; singles, 2 hidden singles, 3 pointing pairs, 4 beyond the three. An instance is its puzzle
; transformed by the seed and the instance's number: the bands permuted and the rows within
; each band, the stacks and the columns within each stack, a transposition, and the values
; relabeled. Each is a symmetry of the rules, so the instance keeps its puzzle's one solution
; and its grade.
;
; How it settles. The cartridge says (settle 16): after an act the engine steps the board
; again, with no act, until a frame changes nothing (docs/SPEC.md section 5, version 6). An
; act is three frames, its own, the one after the engine releases its command, and one that
; proves nothing moved; the load settles too, so the board opens on its values.
;
; What a rule costs (docs/SPEC.md section 2), and how this source keeps it:
;   - The language counts with SUM over ranges, and holds no COUNTIF for a cartridge, so the
;     constraints are counted from nine planes of ones and zeros: a unit's count of a value
;     is a SUM over a plane's row, column or box, read by the unit's nine variables.
;   - A command is read once, in a cell of the Lab, and every variable reads that cell.
;   - The marks' text is built by & and never compared.

(cartridge "seiyaku"
  (spec 6)                          ; the version of docs/SPEC.md this cartridge is written to: an act's place, (settle K) and (bound ...)
  (title "Seiyaku 制約")            ; what the host shows: the name and its kanji, "constraints"
  (rate 0)                          ; an act steps the board; nothing else does
  (screen grid 9 9)                 ; the Screen, hidden: the Camera shows the Board in its place
  (seed host)                       ; the host's seed, new instances each load; a seed typed into Clock!B3 brings them back
  (settle 16)                       ; an act's settle, at most 16 steps
  (bound "Board")                   ; the Board drawn to its extent and no further
  (author "Spreadsheet Company")    ; who wrote it
  (license "0BSD")                  ; the header's twin: copy this file to start a game of your own
  (notes "Seiyaku 制約: eighty-one variables, twenty-seven constraints, one solution, proven before you began. 1 to 9, the row's or the keypad's, assign a value to the variable the selection stands on and Backspace retracts it; Q W E, A S D and Z X C mark a value in its domain, each key where its mark stands in the cell; F fills every unassigned domain with the values its constraints allow; R retracts every assignment, N deals a new instance and G sets the next instance's grade."))

; The library whose macros this source calls: sheets, labels and headers; cells, rules
; and on, each naming a sheet once over a run of its rows; rule; count and first-frame;
; camera; and picture, which writes the book. Since KIT.5 every rule is written as
; expressions, which the formula syntax writes to the same bytes: a reference computed
; from a number is a ref into its sheet, or, on the rule's own sheet, a symbol fused from
; its letters and its row.
(include "../common.vla")

; ---- the sheets, in tab order ----------------------------------------------------------
; The Board and the Constraints a person sees; the rest hidden, each a layer of the rule.
(sheets "Board" "Constraints")
(sheet "Book" hidden)
(sheet "Deal" hidden)
(sheet "Givens" hidden)
(sheet "Entries" hidden)
(sheet "Marks" hidden)
(sheet "Grid" hidden)
(sheet "Planes" hidden)
(sheet "Units" hidden)
(sheet "Candidates" hidden)
(sheet "Violations" hidden)
(sheet "Lab" hidden)
(sheet "Screen" hidden)
(sheet "Camera" hidden)
(sheet "Commands" hidden)

; ---- the Camera: the Board shown in the Screen's place (docs/SPEC.md section 3.8) --------
(camera 1 1)
(cells "Camera" ("A3" "sheet") ("B3" "Board"))

; ---- the commands (docs/SPEC.md section 3.10), each a key on the viewport at rate 0 ----
; Empty holds hold always. A command on a variable stands on the cell the selection stands
; on, and touches nothing on another sheet; domains, retract-all, instance and grade act
; from any sheet.
(headers "Commands" "A1" "name" "words" "holds" "key")
(cells "Commands"
  ("A2" "assign-1")    ("B2" "assign 1 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D2" "Digit1")
  ("A3" "assign-2")    ("B3" "assign 2 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D3" "Digit2")
  ("A4" "assign-3")    ("B4" "assign 3 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D4" "Digit3")
  ("A5" "assign-4")    ("B5" "assign 4 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D5" "Digit4")
  ("A6" "assign-5")    ("B6" "assign 5 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D6" "Digit5")
  ("A7" "assign-6")    ("B7" "assign 6 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D7" "Digit6")
  ("A8" "assign-7")    ("B8" "assign 7 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D8" "Digit7")
  ("A9" "assign-8")    ("B9" "assign 8 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it")  ("D9" "Digit8")
  ("A10" "assign-9")   ("B10" "assign 9 to the variable the selection stands on, unless the instance fixes it") ("D10" "Digit9")
  ("A11" "retract")    ("B11" "retract the variable's assignment; on an unassigned variable, strike every mark") ("D11" "Backspace")
  ("A12" "domain-1")   ("B12" "mark 1 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D12" "KeyQ")
  ("A13" "domain-2")   ("B13" "mark 2 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D13" "KeyW")
  ("A14" "domain-3")   ("B14" "mark 3 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D14" "KeyE")
  ("A15" "domain-4")   ("B15" "mark 4 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D15" "KeyA")
  ("A16" "domain-5")   ("B16" "mark 5 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D16" "KeyS")
  ("A17" "domain-6")   ("B17" "mark 6 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D17" "KeyD")
  ("A18" "domain-7")   ("B18" "mark 7 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D18" "KeyZ")
  ("A19" "domain-8")   ("B19" "mark 8 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D19" "KeyX")
  ("A20" "domain-9")   ("B20" "mark 9 in the variable's domain, or strike it")                                   ("D20" "KeyC")
  ("A21" "domains")    ("B21" "fill every unassigned variable's domain with the values its constraints still allow") ("D21" "KeyF")
  ("A22" "retract-all") ("B22" "retract every assignment and strike every mark of the instance")                 ("D22" "KeyR")
  ("A23" "instance")   ("B23" "deal a new instance, at the next instance's grade")                               ("D23" "KeyN")
  ("A24" "grade")      ("B24" "the next instance's grade: 1, 2, 3, 4 and round")                                 ("D24" "KeyG"))

; ---- the Lab: the counts, and the act read once ---------------------------------------
; The acts of this instance, the instances dealt, the restarts; the next instance's grade,
; 2 at the load, and this instance's; the act's value, its mark, a retraction, the domains
; filled, and the variable it stands on, 1 to 81 or 0; satisfied, and the acts it took.
(labels "Lab" "A1" "acts" "instances" "restarts" "next grade" "grade" "assigned" "marked" "retract" "domains" "place" "satisfied" "satisfied in")
(defmacro (a-command word)
  "the command named by the word, run at this frame: Input!$B$20=\"word\""
  (= Input!$B$20 word))
(defmacro (named-as prefix k)
  "a command's value when it is the prefix and k, assign-k or domain-k: (Input!$B$20=\"prefix-k\")*k"
  (* (a-command (&expand prefix k)) k))
(rules "Lab"
  ("B1" (if (or (<> Lab!B2 Lab.last!B2) (<> Lab!B3 Lab.last!B3)) 0 (+ Lab.last!B1 (if (or (= Input!$B$13 1) (= Input!$B$14 1) (= Input!$B$15 1) (<> Input!$B$20 "")) 1 0)))))
(count "Lab" "B2" (if (a-command "instance") 1 0))
(count "Lab" "B3" (if (a-command "retract-all") 1 0))
(first-frame "Lab" "B4" 2 (if (a-command "grade") (+ (mod Lab.last!B4 4) 1) Lab.last!B4))
(rules "Lab"
  ("B5" (if (or (= Clock!$B$1 1) (<> Lab!B2 Lab.last!B2)) Lab!B4 Lab.last!B5))
  ("B6" (+ (named-as "assign-" 1) (named-as "assign-" 2) (named-as "assign-" 3) (named-as "assign-" 4) (named-as "assign-" 5) (named-as "assign-" 6) (named-as "assign-" 7) (named-as "assign-" 8) (named-as "assign-" 9)))
  ("B7" (+ (named-as "domain-" 1) (named-as "domain-" 2) (named-as "domain-" 3) (named-as "domain-" 4) (named-as "domain-" 5) (named-as "domain-" 6) (named-as "domain-" 7) (named-as "domain-" 8) (named-as "domain-" 9)))
  ("B8" (if (a-command "retract") 1 0))
  ("B9" (if (a-command "domains") 1 0))
  ("B10" (if (and (= Input!$B$19 "Board") (>= Input!$B$11 1) (<= Input!$B$11 9) (>= Input!$B$12 1) (<= Input!$B$12 9)) (+ (* (- Input!$B$12 1) 9) Input!$B$11) 0))
  ("B11" (if (and (= (sum Planes!A1:I81) 81) (= (sum Violations!A1:I9) 0)) 1 0))
  ("B12" (if (= Lab!B11 1) (if (= Lab.last!B11 1) Lab.last!B12 Lab!B1) 0)))

; ---- the Deal: the instance's puzzle, and its transform --------------------------------
; Rows 10 to 44 hash the seed, the instance and the row: Life's soup hash, two linear forms
; modulo the prime multiplied, every product under 2^53. Each hash times 64 and its row is a
; key no other equals, and a key's rank among its group's is a permutation: the values
; (rows 11 to 19), the bands (20 to 22), each band's rows (23 to 31), the stacks (32 to 34)
; and each stack's columns (35 to 43). Row 10 names the puzzle in its grade's block of the
; book and row 44 whether the instance is transposed. F1:F9 hold each row's source row and
; G1:G9 each column's source column; A50:CC50 the puzzle's 81 values.
(labels "Deal" "A1" "puzzle" "transposed")
(headers "Deal" "B9" "hash" "key" "rank")
(rules "Deal"
  ("B1" (+ (* 32 (- Lab!$B$5 1)) 1 (mod B10 32)))
  ("B2" (mod B44 2))
  ("F1:F9" (+ (* 3 (- (choose (+ (int (/ (- (row) 1) 3)) 1) $D$20 $D$21 $D$22) 1)) D23))
  ("G1:G9" (+ (* 3 (- (choose (+ (int (/ (- (row) 1) 3)) 1) $D$32 $D$33 $D$34) 1)) D35))
  ("B10:B44" (mod (* (mod (+ (* Clock!$B$3 1103515) (* Lab!$B$2 7919) (* (row) 1597334) 3440100) 67108859)
                   (mod (+ (* Clock!$B$3 2012345) (* Lab!$B$2 104729) (* (row) 1209487) 3213021) 67108859))
                67108859))
  ("C10:C44" (+ (* B10 64) (row)))
  ("D11:D19" (+ 1 (< C$11 C11) (< C$12 C11) (< C$13 C11) (< C$14 C11) (< C$15 C11) (< C$16 C11) (< C$17 C11) (< C$18 C11) (< C$19 C11))))

(defmacro (ranks-of-three first)
  "the ranks of three keys among themselves, from the first's row: a band's, a stack's, or a band's or a stack's three"
  (rule "Deal" (&expand "D" first ":D" (+expand first 2))
    (+ 1 (< (symbol "C$" first) (symbol "C" first)) (< (symbol "C$" (+expand first 1)) (symbol "C" first)) (< (symbol "C$" (+expand first 2)) (symbol "C" first)))))
(ranks-of-three 20)                 ; the bands
(ranks-of-three 23)                 ; the first band's rows
(ranks-of-three 26)                 ; the second band's rows
(ranks-of-three 29)                 ; the third band's rows
(ranks-of-three 32)                 ; the stacks
(ranks-of-three 35)                 ; the first stack's columns
(ranks-of-three 38)                 ; the second stack's columns
(ranks-of-three 41)                 ; the third stack's columns

; The puzzle's 81 values: each column of the Book, as the puzzle's row chooses it. A walk
; gathers the Book's 128 rows of a column as references, from the last down to the first,
; each consed before the ones gathered, and hands the list on to the macro that writes the
; row, which splices it into CHOOSE's arguments, since a macro's call is no argument of a
; primitive.
(defmacro (book-refs k made then)
  "the Book's column A from row k down to row 1, each a reference consed before made, handed on: (then refs)"
  (quote-if (<expand k 1)
    (quasiquote ((unquote then) (unquote made)))
    (quasiquote (book-refs (unquote (-expand k 1)) (unquote (cons (symbol "Book!A" k) made)) (unquote then)))))
(defmacro (chosen-row refs)
  "the puzzle's 81 values, a row of the Deal: CHOOSE over the Book's column, by the puzzle's row"
  (quasiquote (rule "Deal" "A50:CC50" (choose $B$1 (unquote-splicing refs)))))
(book-refs 127 (Book!A128) chosen-row)

; ---- the Givens: the puzzle transformed ------------------------------------------------
; A11:I19, each variable's value in the puzzle, its source the puzzle's row and column its
; own row's and column's sources, swapped when transposed; A1:I9, that value relabeled; and
; A21:I29, 1 where the instance fixes a value.
(defmacro (chosen-refs k made then)
  "the Deal's 81 values from the kth down to the first, each a reference consed before made, handed on: (then refs)"
  (quote-if (<expand k 1)
    (quasiquote ((unquote then) (unquote made)))
    (quasiquote (chosen-refs (unquote (-expand k 1)) (unquote (cons (symbol "Deal!$" (column-letters-expand k) "$50") made)) (unquote then)))))
(defmacro (source-cells refs)
  "each variable's value in the puzzle, read from the Deal's 81 at its source: the row's source times nine and the column's, swapped when transposed"
  (quasiquote (rule "Givens" "A11:I19"
    (choose (if (= Deal!$B$2 1)
                (+ (* (- (choose (column) Deal!$F$1 Deal!$F$2 Deal!$F$3 Deal!$F$4 Deal!$F$5 Deal!$F$6 Deal!$F$7 Deal!$F$8 Deal!$F$9) 1) 9) Deal!$G1)
                (+ (* (- Deal!$F1 1) 9) (choose (column) Deal!$G$1 Deal!$G$2 Deal!$G$3 Deal!$G$4 Deal!$G$5 Deal!$G$6 Deal!$G$7 Deal!$G$8 Deal!$G$9)))
            (unquote-splicing refs)))))
(chosen-refs 80 (Deal!$CC$50) source-cells)
(rules "Givens"
  ("A1:I9" (if (= A11 0) 0 (choose A11 Deal!$D$11 Deal!$D$12 Deal!$D$13 Deal!$D$14 Deal!$D$15 Deal!$D$16 Deal!$D$17 Deal!$D$18 Deal!$D$19)))
  ("A21:I29" (if (> A1 0) 1 0)))

; ---- the person's state: the assignments and the marks -----------------------------------
; Each variable a formula of its own last value and the act (CART.14, decision 2): a new
; instance or a restart empties it; a given is never assigned or marked; an act on it assigns
; a value, retracts, or marks a value, an assigned variable's marks kept and none changed;
; domains fills every unassigned variable's marks with its candidates, Candidates!A83:I91.
; A mark is a bit: the marks are one number, 1 for the 1, 2 for the 2, 256 for the 9.
(defmacro (a-new-instance)
  "a new instance or a restart this frame: the instances or the restarts counted moved"
  (or (<> Lab!$B$2 Lab.last!$B$2) (<> Lab!$B$3 Lab.last!$B$3)))
(defmacro (this-variable)
  "the variable this cell is, 1 to 81, as the Lab numbers the act's place"
  (+ (* (- (row) 1) 9) (column)))
(defmacro (the-mark)
  "the bit of the value the act marks: 2 to the value less one"
  (^ 2 (- Lab!$B$7 1)))
(defmacro (bit-of cell k)
  "a bit of a number of marks: the number over k, 2 to the mark's place, whole and modulo 2"
  (mod (int (/ cell k)) 2))
(rule "Entries" "A1:I9"
  (if (a-new-instance) 0                                           ; a new instance or a restart empties it;
    (if (> Givens!A1 0) 0                                          ; a given is never assigned;
      (if (= Lab!$B$10 (this-variable))                            ; an act on it
          (if (> Lab!$B$6 0) Lab!$B$6 (if (= Lab!$B$8 1) 0 Entries.last!A1))   ;   assigns a value, or retracts;
          Entries.last!A1))))                                      ; else as it was
(rule "Marks" "A1:I9"
  (if (a-new-instance) 0                                           ; a new instance or a restart strikes every mark;
    (if (> Givens!A1 0) 0                                          ; a given is never marked;
      (if (= Lab!$B$9 1) (if (> Entries!A1 0) Marks.last!A1 Candidates!A83)   ; domains fills an unassigned variable's marks with its candidates;
        (if (= Lab!$B$10 (this-variable))                          ; an act on it
            (if (and (> Lab!$B$7 0) (= Entries!A1 0))              ;   marks a value in an unassigned variable, or strikes it,
                (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks.last!A1 (the-mark))) 2) 1) (- Marks.last!A1 (the-mark)) (+ Marks.last!A1 (the-mark)))
                (if (and (= Lab!$B$8 1) (= Entries.last!A1 0)) 0 Marks.last!A1))   ;   and a retraction of an unassigned variable strikes every mark;
            Marks.last!A1)))))                                     ; else as it was
(rule "Marks" "A11:I19"
  (+ (mod A1 2) (bit-of A1 2) (bit-of A1 4) (bit-of A1 8) (bit-of A1 16) (bit-of A1 32) (bit-of A1 64) (bit-of A1 128) (bit-of A1 256)))
(rule "Grid" "A1:I9" (+ Givens!A1 Entries!A1))

; ---- the constraints counted (CART.14, decision 5) ------------------------------------------
; Nine planes of ones and zeros, plane v 1 where the Grid holds v, at rows 9 (v - 1) + 1 to 9 v.
(defmacro (planes v)
  "the plane of the value v, then the planes after it"
  (quote-if (>expand v 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (rule "Planes" (&expand "A" (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1) ":I" (*expand 9 v)) (if (= Grid!A1 v) 1 0))
      (quasiquote (planes (unquote (+expand v 1)))))))
(planes 1)

; The Units: A1:I9 each row's count of each value, a row a row and a value a column;
; A11:I19 each column's, a value a row and a column a column; A21:I29 each box's, a box a row
; and a value a column.
(defmacro (row-counts v)
  "each row's count of the value v, down the column v, then the values after it"
  (quote-if (>expand v 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (rule "Units" (&expand (column-letters-expand v) "1:" (column-letters-expand v) "9")
        (sum (ref "Planes" (&expand "$A" (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1) ":$I" (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1)))))
      (quasiquote (row-counts (unquote (+expand v 1)))))))
(row-counts 1)
(defmacro (col-counts v)
  "each column's count of the value v, along the row 10 + v, then the values after it"
  (quote-if (>expand v 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (rule "Units" (&expand "A" (+expand 10 v) ":I" (+expand 10 v))
        (sum (ref "Planes" (&expand "A" (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1) ":A" (*expand 9 v)))))
      (quasiquote (col-counts (unquote (+expand v 1)))))))
(col-counts 1)
(defmacro (box-counts b r0 c0 v)
  "the box b's count of each value from v, its top left at the row r0 and the column c0 of each plane"
  (quote-if (>expand v 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (rule "Units" (address-expand (+expand 20 b) v)
        (sum (ref "Planes" (&expand (address-expand (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) r0) c0) ":" (address-expand (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) (+expand r0 2)) (+expand c0 2))))))
      (quasiquote (box-counts (unquote b) (unquote r0) (unquote c0) (unquote (+expand v 1)))))))
(box-counts 1 1 1 1)                ; box 1, its top left A1
(box-counts 2 1 4 1)                ; box 2, D1
(box-counts 3 1 7 1)                ; box 3, G1
(box-counts 4 4 1 1)                ; box 4, A4
(box-counts 5 4 4 1)                ; box 5, D4
(box-counts 6 4 7 1)                ; box 6, G4
(box-counts 7 7 1 1)                ; box 7, A7
(box-counts 8 7 4 1)                ; box 8, D7
(box-counts 9 7 7 1)                ; box 9, G7

; A variable is violated where its value counts twice in its row, its column or its box,
; each count read through CHOOSE over the nine values. A fill a box, since a box's counts
; stand on a row of the Units of their own.
(defmacro (unit-count letters r)
  "a cell of the Units, a reference from its column's letters and its row"
  (ref "Units" (&expand letters r)))
(defmacro (row-count-of at r)
  "the count of the variable's value in its row: CHOOSE over the Units' row r, the value the index"
  (choose (ref "Grid" at) (unit-count "$A" r) (unit-count "$B" r) (unit-count "$C" r) (unit-count "$D" r) (unit-count "$E" r) (unit-count "$F" r) (unit-count "$G" r) (unit-count "$H" r) (unit-count "$I" r)))
(defmacro (column-count-of at c)
  "the count of the variable's value in its column: CHOOSE down the Units' column c, rows 11 to 19"
  (choose (ref "Grid" at) (unit-count c "$11") (unit-count c "$12") (unit-count c "$13") (unit-count c "$14") (unit-count c "$15") (unit-count c "$16") (unit-count c "$17") (unit-count c "$18") (unit-count c "$19")))
(defmacro (box-count-of at x)
  "the count of the variable's value in its box: CHOOSE over the Units' row x, the box's own"
  (choose (ref "Grid" at) (unit-count "$A$" x) (unit-count "$B$" x) (unit-count "$C$" x) (unit-count "$D$" x) (unit-count "$E$" x) (unit-count "$F$" x) (unit-count "$G$" x) (unit-count "$H$" x) (unit-count "$I$" x)))
(defmacro (violation-box range at r c x)
  "the box over range: its first cell at, that cell's row r and column c, the box's counts on the Units' row x"
  (rule "Violations" range
    (if (= (ref "Grid" at) 0) 0
      (if (or (> (row-count-of at r) 1) (> (column-count-of at c) 1) (> (box-count-of at x) 1)) 1 0))))
(violation-box "A1:C3" "A1" 1 "A" 21)
(violation-box "D1:F3" "D1" 1 "D" 22)
(violation-box "G1:I3" "G1" 1 "G" 23)
(violation-box "A4:C6" "A4" 4 "A" 24)
(violation-box "D4:F6" "D4" 4 "D" 25)
(violation-box "G4:I6" "G4" 4 "G" 26)
(violation-box "A7:C9" "A7" 7 "A" 27)
(violation-box "D7:F9" "D7" 7 "D" 28)
(violation-box "G7:I9" "G7" 7 "G" 29)

; A value is a candidate of an unassigned variable where it counts in none of its three
; constraints: nine planes like the Planes', each a fill; A83:I91 the candidates as marks.
(defmacro (candidate-planes v)
  "the candidates of the value v, then the values after it"
  (quote-if (>expand v 9)
    (begin)
    (quasiquote
      (begin
        (candidate-plane (unquote (column-letters-expand v)) (unquote (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1)) (unquote (*expand 9 v)) (unquote (+expand 10 v)))
        (candidate-planes (unquote (+expand v 1)))))))
(defmacro (box-count-in letter top)
  "the value's count in the variable's box, the plane's rows from top: CHOOSE over the Units' box rows, 21 to 29, in the value's column letter"
  (choose (+ (* 3 (int (/ (- (row) top) 3))) (int (/ (- (column) 1) 3)) 1) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 21) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 22) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 23) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 24) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 25) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 26) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 27) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 28) (unit-count (&expand "$" letter "$") 29)))
(defmacro (candidate-plane letter top bottom units-row)
  "a plane of candidates from the row top to the row bottom: the value's counts in the Units' column letter, its columns' on units-row"
  (rule "Candidates" (&expand "A" top ":I" bottom)
    (if (and (= Grid!A1 0) (= (unit-count (&expand "$" letter) 1) 0) (= (unit-count "A$" units-row) 0) (= (box-count-in letter top) 0)) 1 0)))
(candidate-planes 1)
(rule "Candidates" "A83:I91"
  (+ A1 (* 2 A10) (* 4 A19) (* 8 A28) (* 16 A37) (* 32 A46) (* 64 A55) (* 128 A64) (* 256 A73)))

; ---- the Board: what a person sees -------------------------------------------------------
; An assigned variable shows a code, 100 times its kind, 10 times its box's parity and its
; value: the kinds a given (1), an assignment (2), a violated given (3), a violated
; assignment (4), and, once satisfied, a given (5) and an assignment (6); the parity 0 on the
; boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9 and 1 on the others. Each code draws through a look. An unassigned
; variable shows its marks, a digit or a figure space in each of nine places, three figure
; spaces between two of a line and a figure space before each, which its own format wraps
; into five lines, three of marks and a line of a figure space between two; or nothing.
(rule "Board" "A1:I9"
  (if (> Grid!A1 0) (+ (if (= Lab!$B$11 1) (if (> Givens!A1 0) 500 600) (if (> Givens!A1 0) (if (= Violations!A1 1) 300 100) (if (= Violations!A1 1) 400 200))) (* 10 (mod (+ (int (/ (- (row) 1) 3)) (int (/ (- (column) 1) 3))) 2)) Grid!A1)
    (if (= Marks!A1 0) ""
      (& " " (if (= (mod Marks!A1 2) 1) "1" " ") "   "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 2)) 2) 1) "2" " ") "   "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 4)) 2) 1) "3" " ") "    "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 8)) 2) 1) "4" " ") "   "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 16)) 2) 1) "5" " ") "   "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 32)) 2) 1) "6" " ") "    "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 64)) 2) 1) "7" " ") "   "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 128)) 2) 1) "8" " ") "   "
         (if (= (mod (int (/ Marks!A1 256)) 2) 1) "9" " ")))))

; Each variable's own format, its box's tint and a wrap, which draws its marks: the format 1
; on the boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9, the format 2 on the others. A style row names one cell.
(defmacro (board-styles r c)
  "the variables' own formats, row by row from the row r and the column c"
  (quote-if (>expand r 9)
    (begin)
    (quote-if (>expand c 9)
      (quasiquote (board-styles (unquote (+expand r 1)) 1))
      (begin
        (style "Board" (address-expand r c) (+expand 1 (mod-expand (+expand (quotient-expand (-expand r 1) 3) (quotient-expand (-expand c 1) 3)) 2)))
        (quasiquote (board-styles (unquote r) (unquote (+expand c 1))))))))
(board-styles 1 1)

; A variable 12.57 characters wide and 66 points tall, 88 pixels square, twice the size it
; first had (the owner's hand test, 2026-10-19): a line of marks, ten digits wide, fits it,
; and a line, a space and a figure space do not, so the marks wrap into five lines, the
; first, third and fifth of them marks, in their places.
(defmacro (board-columns c)
  "the Board's columns from the column c, each 12.57 characters wide, 88 pixels"
  (quote-if (>expand c 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (column "Board" (column-letters-expand c) 12.57 shown none)
      (quasiquote (board-columns (unquote (+expand c 1)))))))
(board-columns 1)
(defmacro (board-rows r)
  "the Board's rows from the row r, each 66 points tall, 88 pixels"
  (quote-if (>expand r 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (row "Board" r 66 shown)
      (quasiquote (board-rows (unquote (+expand r 1)))))))
(board-rows 1)

; ---- the look: Lovelace Lavender -------------------------------------------------------------
; A format holds a fill and no font, so the fills say the box and a violation, and the glyph
; says a given: Unicode's mathematical bold digits for a given, plain digits for an
; assignment, each followed by five figure spaces, which center a digit that aligns right.
; The boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9 in a pale lavender, the others white; a violation red, given or
; assigned, Superposition's red; the satisfied board Lovelace Lavender itself, by box.
(format 1 "E8E0F7" general wrap)    ; an unassigned variable on the boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9
(format 2 "FFFFFF" general wrap)    ; an unassigned variable on the others

(defmacro (kind-looks kind fill-even fill-odd glyphs)
  "a kind's eighteen looks: its nine values on the boxes 1, 3, 5, 7 and 9, then on the others"
  (quasiquote
    (begin
      (value-looks (unquote kind) 0 (unquote fill-even) 1 (unquote glyphs))
      (value-looks (unquote kind) 1 (unquote fill-odd) 1 (unquote glyphs)))))
(defmacro (value-looks kind parity tint v glyphs)
  "a look a value from v: the format 2 + 18 (kind - 1) + 9 parity + v, its tint and its glyph centered; the code 100 kind + 10 parity + v"
  (quote-if (null? glyphs)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (format (+expand 2 (+expand (*expand 18 (-expand kind 1)) (+expand (*expand 9 parity) v))) tint (&expand "\"" (car glyphs) "     \"") nowrap)
      (look "Board" (+expand (*expand 100 kind) (+expand (*expand 10 parity) v)) (+expand 2 (+expand (*expand 18 (-expand kind 1)) (+expand (*expand 9 parity) v))))
      (quasiquote (value-looks (unquote kind) (unquote parity) (unquote tint) (unquote (+expand v 1)) (unquote (cdr glyphs)))))))
(kind-looks 1 "E8E0F7" "FFFFFF" ("𝟏" "𝟐" "𝟑" "𝟒" "𝟓" "𝟔" "𝟕" "𝟖" "𝟗"))   ; a given
(kind-looks 2 "E8E0F7" "FFFFFF" ("1" "2" "3" "4" "5" "6" "7" "8" "9"))   ; an assignment
(kind-looks 3 "FFD5D5" "FFD5D5" ("𝟏" "𝟐" "𝟑" "𝟒" "𝟓" "𝟔" "𝟕" "𝟖" "𝟗"))   ; a violated given
(kind-looks 4 "FFD5D5" "FFD5D5" ("1" "2" "3" "4" "5" "6" "7" "8" "9"))   ; a violated assignment
(kind-looks 5 "A080E0" "B9A3E7" ("𝟏" "𝟐" "𝟑" "𝟒" "𝟓" "𝟔" "𝟕" "𝟖" "𝟗"))   ; a given, satisfied
(kind-looks 6 "A080E0" "B9A3E7" ("1" "2" "3" "4" "5" "6" "7" "8" "9"))   ; an assignment, satisfied
(on "Board" (gridlines on))

; ---- the keys, beside the Board (the owner's hand test, 2026-10-19) ---------------------------
; What each key does, a key a row beside the variables: K the key, L its words, both on the
; canvas's gray, the headers' own, which a bound sheet stands on, so that the Board alone is
; white; J a gutter of the same gray. The marks' keys drawn as the marks are, in five lines,
; each key in its mark's place.
(format 111 "F3F3EE" general nowrap)   ; a key or its words
(format 112 "F3F3EE" general wrap)     ; the marks' keys, wrapped into their places
(cells "Board"
  ("K1" "1 to 9") ("L1" "assign the value to the variable, row or keypad")
  ("K2" "Backspace") ("L2" "retract the assignment, or strike the marks")
  ("K3" " Q   W   E    A   S   D    Z   X   C") ("L3" "mark a value in the domain, at its key's place")
  ("K4" "F") ("L4" "fill every domain with what its constraints allow")
  ("K5" "R") ("L5" "retract every assignment and every mark")
  ("K6" "N") ("L6" "deal a new instance")
  ("K7" "G") ("L7" "the next instance's grade, 1 to 4 and round")
  ("K8" "← ↑ → ↓") ("L8" "move the selection, as a click does")
  ("K9" "Ctrl+K") ("L9" "every command, by its name"))
(style "Board" "K1" 111) (style "Board" "L1" 111)
(style "Board" "K2" 111) (style "Board" "L2" 111)
(style "Board" "K3" 112) (style "Board" "L3" 111)
(style "Board" "K4" 111) (style "Board" "L4" 111)
(style "Board" "K5" 111) (style "Board" "L5" 111)
(style "Board" "K6" 111) (style "Board" "L6" 111)
(style "Board" "K7" 111) (style "Board" "L7" 111)
(style "Board" "K8" 111) (style "Board" "L8" 111)
(style "Board" "K9" 111) (style "Board" "L9" 111)
; the gutter's empty cells by its column's format; the keys' column a variable's width, so that
; the marks' keys lie as the marks do; the words' column as wide as the longest words
(on "Board" (column "J" 3 shown 111) (column "K" 12.57 shown none) (column "L" 48 shown none))

; ---- the Constraints: the counts, and each constraint's state -----------------------------
(cells "Constraints"
  ("A1" "Seiyaku 制約")
  ("A2" "Eighty-one variables, twenty-seven constraints, one solution, proven before you began."))
(labels "Constraints" "A4" "instance" "grade" "puzzle in the book" "seed" "next instance's grade")
(defmacro (grade-named grade)
  "a grade's name: the hardest technique its puzzles need"
  (choose grade "naked singles" "hidden singles" "pointing pairs" "beyond the three"))
(rules "Constraints"
  ("B4" (+ Lab!B2 1))
  ("B5" Lab!B5)
  ("C5" (grade-named Lab!B5))
  ("B6" Deal!B1)
  ("B7" Clock!B3)
  ("B8" Lab!B4)
  ("C8" (grade-named Lab!B4)))
(labels "Constraints" "A10" "givens" "assignments" "unassigned" "violated variables" "violated constraints" "marks kept" "acts" "satisfied")
(rules "Constraints"
  ("B10" (sum Givens!A21:I29))
  ("B11" (- (sum Planes!A1:I81) B10))
  ("B12" (- 81 (sum Planes!A1:I81)))
  ("B13" (sum Violations!A1:I9))
  ("B14" (sum D31:D57))
  ("B15" (sum Marks!A11:I19))
  ("B16" Lab!B1)
  ("B17" (if (= Lab!B11 1) (& "satisfied, in " Lab!B12 " acts") "not yet"))
  ("B18" (if (= Lab!B11 1) "No search was performed by the cartridge." "")))

; Each value's count on the board, 9 of each when satisfied, a value a row.
(headers "Constraints" "A19" "value" "placed")
(labels "Constraints" "A20" 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9)
(defmacro (placed-counts v)
  "the board's count of the value v, a SUM over its plane, then the values after it"
  (quote-if (>expand v 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (rule "Constraints" (address-expand (+expand 19 v) 2)
        (sum (ref "Planes" (&expand "A" (+expand (*expand 9 (-expand v 1)) 1) ":I" (*expand 9 v)))))
      (quasiquote (placed-counts (unquote (+expand v 1)))))))
(placed-counts 1)

; The twenty-seven constraints: each its variables assigned and its state, violated where a
; value counts twice, satisfied where nine are assigned and none is violated, open else.
(headers "Constraints" "A30" "constraint" "assigned" "state" "violated")
(labels "Constraints" "A31"
  "row 1" "row 2" "row 3" "row 4" "row 5" "row 6" "row 7" "row 8" "row 9"
  "column 1" "column 2" "column 3" "column 4" "column 5" "column 6" "column 7" "column 8" "column 9"
  "box 1" "box 2" "box 3" "box 4" "box 5" "box 6" "box 7" "box 8" "box 9")
(defmacro (state-of counts assigned)
  "a constraint's state from its counts and its variables assigned: violated where a value counts twice, satisfied where nine are assigned and none is violated, open else"
  (if (> (max counts) 1) "violated" (if (= assigned 9) "satisfied" "open")))
(rules "Constraints"
  ("B31:B39" (sum Units!$A1:$I1))
  ("C31:C39" (state-of Units!$A1:$I1 B31))
  ("B49:B57" (sum Units!$A21:$I21))
  ("C49:C57" (state-of Units!$A21:$I21 B49))
  ("D31:D57" (if (= C31 "violated") 1 0)))
(defmacro (column-constraints c)
  "the column c's constraint, on the row 39 + c: its count down the Units' column c, rows 11 to 19, then the columns after it"
  (quote-if (>expand c 9)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (rule "Constraints" (address-expand (+expand 39 c) 2)
        (sum (ref "Units" (&expand (column-letters-expand c) "11:" (column-letters-expand c) "19"))))
      (rule "Constraints" (address-expand (+expand 39 c) 3)
        (state-of (ref "Units" (&expand (column-letters-expand c) "11:" (column-letters-expand c) "19")) (symbol "B" (+expand 39 c))))
      (quasiquote (column-constraints (unquote (+expand c 1)))))))
(column-constraints 1)
; Column B twelve characters wide, so that a seed of ten digits, which a person reads off to share an instance, reads
; whole (Superposition's catch at CART.12's hand test).
(on "Constraints" (column "A" 22 shown none) (column "B" 12 shown none) (column "C" 18 shown none))

; ---- the book ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
